From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 147/147] PC5: an ASF video keeps its frame rate, so Resident Evil 2's
 films play (Wine patch 1013)

PC5's FFmpeg parser gave every ASF stream a frame rate of 0/1, as GStreamer's did; native's gives one, and Resident Evil 2 crashed reading it at its first film. The file's own rate is kept, or FFmpeg's guess while it is a real frame rate.
---
 ...keeps-the-frame-rate-its-file-states.patch | 31 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 wine/patches/1013-winegstreamer-an-asf-video-keeps-the-frame-rate-its-file-states.patch

diff --git a/wine/patches/1013-winegstreamer-an-asf-video-keeps-the-frame-rate-its-file-states.patch b/wine/patches/1013-winegstreamer-an-asf-video-keeps-the-frame-rate-its-file-states.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1cbcd71
--- /dev/null
+++ b/wine/patches/1013-winegstreamer-an-asf-video-keeps-the-frame-rate-its-file-states.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
+Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] winegstreamer: An ASF video keeps the frame rate its file
+ states, or FFmpeg's guess when it is one.
+
+Native's ASF source gives a WMV stream a frame rate; this one gave every ASF stream 0/1, and Resident Evil 2 crashes reading the frame rate of its films (its cutscenes played once the WMV went to winedmo with DisableGstByteStreamHandler). FFmpeg's average comes from the file's extended stream properties; without it, its guess is kept up to 240 frames a second, so the millisecond clock's 1000 is still none.
+---
+ dlls/winegstreamer/ffmpeg_parser.c | 9 +++++++--
+ 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
+
+diff --git a/dlls/winegstreamer/ffmpeg_parser.c b/dlls/winegstreamer/ffmpeg_parser.c
+index ec3506f..b39d495 100644
+--- a/dlls/winegstreamer/ffmpeg_parser.c
++++ b/dlls/winegstreamer/ffmpeg_parser.c
+@@ -340,8 +340,13 @@ static struct wg_parser_stream *create_stream(struct wg_parser *parser, AVStream
+     stream->skip_until = INT64_MIN;
+ 
+     fps = av->avg_frame_rate.num > 0 && av->avg_frame_rate.den > 0 ? av->avg_frame_rate : av->r_frame_rate;
+-    /* An ASF file states no frame rate; FFmpeg's is a guess. */
+-    if (!strcmp(parser->format->iformat->name, "asf"))
++    /* An ASF file states its frame rate only in its extended stream properties (FFmpeg's
++     * average); without them FFmpeg's guess is kept while it is a frame rate a video has, as
++     * native's ASF source gives one: Resident Evil 2 reads the rate of its WMV films and
++     * crashes on 0/1. A guess from the file's millisecond clock (1000) is still none. */
++    if (!strcmp(parser->format->iformat->name, "asf")
++            && !(av->avg_frame_rate.num > 0 && av->avg_frame_rate.den > 0)
++            && !(fps.num > 0 && fps.den > 0 && av_q2d(fps) <= 240.0))
+         fps = (AVRational){0, 1};
+     stream->has_codec_format = !is_raw_codec(par->codec_id) && wg_format_from_codec(&stream->codec_format, par, fps);
+ 
